WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.250
Hi!

2
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.829
This is the story of Reminders:

3
00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:09.070
how a simple task list grew, one idea at a time, into a personal assistant.

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.039
It started here:

5
00:00:11.039 --> 00:00:12.783
a plain task reminder.

6
00:00:12.783 --> 00:00:21.030
Add a task with a time, a priority and a repeat, and it chimes when it's due, on a PC or as a phone app.

7
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.086
Then my author, Deiva Prakash, had an idea:

8
00:00:25.086 --> 00:00:28.441
what if I could just talk to it, like Siri?

9
00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:30.705
So a voice assistant arrived.

10
00:00:30.705 --> 00:00:37.260
Say, remind me to call the plumber at six, and it understands, and answers out loud.

11
00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.195
He wanted it to look professional:

12
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:48.280
a side panel with a live twelve-hour clock, smart lists like Today, Overdue and History, and folders for Personal and Work.

13
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.640
Secrets go into a password-protected Private folder, encrypted on the device.

14
00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.910
Plus a to-do list, a Things to Do board with drag-and-drop cards, and a notepad.

15
00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.383
Then Deiva Prakash asked:

16
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:05.865
what would make it truly effective?

17
00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:10.830
Version three added a calendar, where you drag reminders to a new day,

18
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:16.910
habits with streaks, a Pomodoro focus timer, and weekly insights.

19
00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.699
Reminders became hard to miss:

20
00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:27.430
smart snooze, a nagging mode that repeats until it's done, your own alarm sound, and a spoken morning briefing.

21
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:34.015
Each reminder can hold a checklist, photos and files, and even a place, like:

22
00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:35.391
when I leave work.

23
00:01:35.391 --> 00:01:37.990
And it exports to Google Calendar.

24
00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:44.636
The assistant remembers the conversation, so you can just say, move it to eight.

25
00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:50.210
It understands Tamil, and it can ask Claude, an AI model, when it's unsure.

26
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:57.967
An optional server adds push notifications when the app is closed, and encrypted sync between your devices.

27
00:01:57.967 --> 00:02:02.980
There's fingerprint unlock, home-screen shortcuts, and sharing into the app.

28
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.337
From a task list to a personal assistant, built from Deiva Prakash's ideas.

29
00:02:09.337 --> 00:02:12.580
Install it, and never forget a thing again.
